# Technology Diffusion in the &quot;Soft Disciplines&quot;: Using Social Technology to Support Information Technology.

**Authors:** Willis, Jerry

## Abstract
Discusses reasons for the slower acceptance of educational technology in the humanities. Highlights include teacher training; support staff skills; software development; lack of equity in funding for hardware and software; technology diffusion; and a description of the Concerns-Based Adoption Model, a comprehensive model of change in education. (35 references) (LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ461577

